# Combining Horizontal & Vertical

For top‑down or 3D movement, combine two axes into a Vector2 or Vector3:

```csharp
float h = Input.GetAxis("Horizontal");
float v = Input.GetAxis("Vertical");
Vector3 movement = new Vector3(h, 0, v) * speed * Time.deltaTime;
transform.Translate(movement);
```

This moves your object along X and Z (horizontal plane). For 2D, you may use X and Y.
